{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-18\nattempt=1\nbase=d088d3ef8892588e7089c8b4d20b600d4624cb7a\ncandidate=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-18 — SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds the Huddle SPA settings surface on top of the MARATHON-16 shell: a **workspace settings modal** (tabs General / Members / Invitations) and a **channel settings modal** (members list/add, topic, archive/unarchive). It wires those UIs to the already-shipped REST seams from MARATHON-6/7/12 (`PATCH` workspace, members/roles/transfer, invitations create/list/revoke/accept, channel members/topic/archive) and locks the epic’s stable DOM ids plus `settings-*` / `invitation-*` / role / channel-member `data-testid`s so CUA/Playwright can drive admin flows at 1280×900. It also specifies the missing **channel add-member** REST seam that MARATHON-7 deferred, because the channel-settings “add” control cannot work against join alone for private channels.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Delivery | Extend the **zero-build vanilla SPA** (`static/` ES modules) — same stack as MARATHON-16; no bundler |\n| Module split | New `static/js/settings_ui.js` owns both modals; `shell.js` exposes open triggers + active workspace/channel; reuse `api.js` / `storage.js` |\n| Modal pattern | Match `auth-modal`: overlay + panel, `hidden` attribute, `role=\"dialog\"`, Escape/close dismiss; **one settings modal open at a time** |\n| Workspace entry | `data-testid=\"workspace-settings-btn\"` in `workspace-header` (visible whenever shell shows a workspace) |\n| Channel entry | Selecting a non-DM channel in `channel-list` sets active channel; `data-testid=\"channel-settings-btn\"` in message-pane header chrome (or beside channel list) opens channel settings for that id — **does not** require MARATHON-17 message composer |\n| Tabs | Workspace modal: exactly three tabs — `general`, `members`, `invitations`; only one panel visible |\n| Authz UX | Client **hides/disables** privileged controls from cached caller role; server remains SoT (403/404 still shown as `error.message`) |\n| Invitation redeem | Onboarding gains an **accept-by-code** form (M12 assigned redeem UX to this task); settings tab is create/list/revoke only |\n| Channel add-member | New backend seam `POST /api/channels/{id}/members` (this design owns the contract); frontend labeled implementer may land the thin route or a tiny backend follow-up must land first — see Sequencing |\n| Selectors | Exact strings below; prefer `data-testid`; required **DOM ids**: `workspace-settings-modal`, `channel-settings-modal`, `create-invitation-form` |\n\n### Why\n\n- Epic requires settings + invitations in the SPA with stable selectors; M16 explicitly deferred settings modals here.\n- Backend contracts for name/join_mode, roles, invitations, topic, archive, channel member list are closed (M6/7/12); inventing alternate envelopes would break graders and sibling designs.\n- M7’s neighborhood note already flagged `channel-add-member-*` without REST — shipping UI without an add seam leaves private-channel “add” untestable.\n- Keeping vanilla modules preserves `start.sh` / no-Node ops.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Fold settings into MARATHON-17 message chrome only | Blocks settings QA until messages land; task is independent with `frontend` label |\n| “Add member” = tell user to `POST .../join` | Fails for private channels (403 without membership); hooks expect add controls |\n| Profile PATCH inside General tab | Task tabs are name/join_mode/members/invitations only; profile is a different surface |\n| Groups CRUD UI | MARATHON-12 groups API exists but is not in this task description |\n| React settings app | Diverges from M16 zero-build convention |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nChannel add-member needs a **small backend POST** that did not ship in M7. This design locks that seam so SPA and server can be implemented in parallel; if the implementer is frontend-only, the lead should keep `frontend` and optionally add a short backend subtask — **do not** fake\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=6c6170f7b7fb6d4ccb358c5af71c7031f3d20512 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"b1a711f5-57c8-440e-a73c-5e4a0bd4f824"}
